1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,900
The first time I heard my own voice
on channel nine, it was begging me

2
00:00:03,925 --> 00:00:05,462
not to open the door.

3
00:00:05,488 --> 00:00:07,688
Not a voice that sounded like mine.

4
00:00:07,712 --> 00:00:11,300
Mine. The same breathless catch
I get when I try not to panic.

5
00:00:11,325 --> 00:00:12,288
Then somebody knocked.

6
00:00:12,312 --> 00:00:13,750
Three slow knocks.

7
00:00:13,775 --> 00:00:17,162
I was alone at Blackpine Relay, a
little communications station above

8
00:00:17,188 --> 00:00:18,725
thirty miles of forest.

9
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:20,950
My shift had started an hour earlier.

10
00:00:20,975 --> 00:00:22,788
I had already done the radio check.

11
00:00:22,812 --> 00:00:24,112
Blackpine Relay.

12
00:00:24,138 --> 00:00:25,288
Daniel Reed.

13
00:00:25,312 --> 00:00:26,463
Night shift.

14
00:00:26,488 --> 00:00:29,802
Now the same speaker was
saying my name back to me.

15
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:32,918
Outside, rain crawled down the window.

16
00:00:32,942 --> 00:00:35,968
Inside, the wall clock
said twelve thirteen.

17
00:00:35,992 --> 00:00:38,643
The voice gave a time four minutes later.

18
00:00:38,668 --> 00:00:40,205
Twelve seventeen.

19
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:43,942
And then it said something I could
not understand until much later.

20
00:00:43,968 --> 00:00:46,495
Whatever happens, don't let her answer.

21
00:00:47,455 --> 00:00:50,755
There was a laminated instruction
card beside the radio.

22
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:54,330
The official side explained
how to log emergency traffic.

23
00:00:54,355 --> 00:00:57,393
On the back, somebody had written
one sentence in black marker.

24
00:00:57,418 --> 00:00:59,555
If you hear yourself, do not answer.

25
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:01,655
I thought it was a joke
left for the new guy.

26
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:03,318
I pressed the microphone anyway.

27
00:01:03,342 --> 00:01:04,305
Who is this?

28
00:01:04,330 --> 00:01:07,055
The red light stayed on
after I released the button.

29
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:09,280
From the speaker came a soft breath.

30
00:01:09,305 --> 00:01:11,680
Then my voice said, You
just made it easier.

31
00:01:11,705 --> 00:01:13,580
I pulled the microphone plug.

32
00:01:13,605 --> 00:01:15,383
The voice continued.

33
00:01:15,935 --> 00:01:18,635
In four minutes you're going
to break the white mug.

34
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:21,460
You're going to find a red
key behind the battery.

35
00:01:21,485 --> 00:01:23,348
And you're going to call your sister.

36
00:01:23,372 --> 00:01:25,697
I looked at the mug beside my hand.

37
00:01:25,722 --> 00:01:28,522
I had not told anyone at work about Lena.

38
00:01:28,548 --> 00:01:31,350
The telephone on the desk began to ring.

39
00:01:32,310 --> 00:01:33,960
I let it ring until it stopped.

40
00:01:33,985 --> 00:01:35,335
The radio clicked.

41
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:36,960
You should have picked up, my voice said.

42
00:01:36,985 --> 00:01:37,910
She thinks you're angry.

43
00:01:37,935 --> 00:01:40,360
I stood so quickly my
chair caught the table.

44
00:01:40,385 --> 00:01:43,035
The mug fell. It struck
the floor in three pieces.

45
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:44,672
The clock said twelve seventeen.

46
00:01:44,698 --> 00:01:45,660
Four minutes.

47
00:01:45,685 --> 00:01:48,235
I told myself somebody
had cameras in the room.

48
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:51,160
That somebody was watching
me and playing a recording.

49
00:01:51,185 --> 00:01:54,910
I searched above the shelves, under
the desk, inside the dead security

50
00:01:54,935 --> 00:01:56,648
monitor. Nothing.

51
00:01:56,673 --> 00:01:59,813
Then I saw the battery at
the back of the radio rack.

52
00:02:00,315 --> 00:02:02,152
Behind it was a red key.

53
00:02:02,178 --> 00:02:04,078
One tooth was broken off.

54
00:02:04,102 --> 00:02:07,002
A little paper tag had gone soft with age.

55
00:02:07,028 --> 00:02:10,477
On it was a drawing of the steel
cabinet in the back hallway.

56
00:02:10,502 --> 00:02:12,752
From outside came another knock.

57
00:02:12,778 --> 00:02:14,728
This time it was at the window.

58
00:02:14,752 --> 00:02:17,530
The glass was ten feet above the ground.

59
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:20,365
I called Lena on the landline.

60
00:02:20,390 --> 00:02:22,677
My cell phone had no service up there.

61
00:02:22,702 --> 00:02:25,115
She answered on the
second ring, half asleep.

62
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:27,165
I told her I needed her
to stay on the phone.

63
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:28,090
Not to drive up.

64
00:02:28,115 --> 00:02:29,115
Just talk.

65
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:32,102
While she asked what was wrong,
the radio made a sound like someone

66
00:02:32,128 --> 00:02:33,377
clearing their throat.

67
00:02:33,402 --> 00:02:35,102
A woman's voice came through.

68
00:02:35,128 --> 00:02:36,402
Lena's voice.

69
00:02:36,427 --> 00:02:39,527
Half a second before she spoke into
the telephone, the radio said the

70
00:02:39,552 --> 00:02:40,677
same words.

71
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:42,090
Daniel, are you hurt?

72
00:02:42,115 --> 00:02:43,127
I hung up.

73
00:02:43,152 --> 00:02:45,068
The radio went silent.

74
00:02:45,570 --> 00:02:48,645
For the first time, the thing
outside stopped knocking.

75
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:51,307
I understood enough to
be afraid of the wires.

76
00:02:51,332 --> 00:02:54,282
The antenna cable ran
through the rear wall.

77
00:02:54,308 --> 00:02:58,182
The telephone cable disappeared
into the same steel cabinet.

78
00:02:58,207 --> 00:03:00,507
I followed them with my flashlight.

79
00:03:00,532 --> 00:03:04,570
Something wet brushed the other side
of the wall, keeping pace with me

80
00:03:04,595 --> 00:03:04,835
.

81
00:03:05,795 --> 00:03:07,682
The red key fitted the cabinet.

82
00:03:07,707 --> 00:03:11,057
Inside were the antenna switch,
the telephone junction, and a small

83
00:03:11,082 --> 00:03:12,557
backup power supply.

84
00:03:12,582 --> 00:03:14,770
Scratched into the metal
was another warning.

85
00:03:14,795 --> 00:03:16,495
It follows the open line.

86
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:18,470
My voice returned from the front room.

87
00:03:18,495 --> 00:03:19,582
Don't touch the antenna.

88
00:03:19,607 --> 00:03:20,695
I'm trying to help you.

89
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:22,370
I turned the switch a quarter turn.

90
00:03:22,395 --> 00:03:24,582
The voice stretched, thin and distant.

91
00:03:24,607 --> 00:03:27,395
Outside, something dragged a
fingernail down the window.

92
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:28,870
I turned the switch back.

93
00:03:28,895 --> 00:03:30,295
The scratching stopped.

94
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:32,270
Then my voice whispered, Look at me.

95
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:33,822
I should not have looked.

96
00:03:34,375 --> 00:03:36,350
A man stood beyond the glass.

97
00:03:36,375 --> 00:03:37,875
My jacket. My haircut.

98
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:38,900
My face.

99
00:03:38,925 --> 00:03:42,337
But he was smiling with his mouth
closed, and the shape of the smile

100
00:03:42,362 --> 00:03:43,950
moved under his skin.

101
00:03:43,975 --> 00:03:46,675
His right hand was
pressed against the glass.

102
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:49,050
I have a scar across my left palm.

103
00:03:49,075 --> 00:03:51,490
His scar was on the wrong hand.

104
00:03:52,450 --> 00:03:53,900
The station lights went out.

105
00:03:53,925 --> 00:03:55,175
The radio did not.

106
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:57,875
Its green lamp burned
on the backup battery.

107
00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:00,075
The man outside tilted his head.

108
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:03,025
In the dark, I heard him speak from
the radio, from the telephone, and

109
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:04,537
from the other side of the window.

110
00:04:04,562 --> 00:04:05,612
All at once.

111
00:04:05,637 --> 00:04:06,900
Cut the power, he said.

112
00:04:06,925 --> 00:04:08,400
I opened the cabinet again.

113
00:04:08,425 --> 00:04:11,187
My flashlight found
two thick black cables.

114
00:04:11,212 --> 00:04:12,850
One fed the antenna.

115
00:04:12,875 --> 00:04:15,037
One fed the telephone junction.

116
00:04:15,062 --> 00:04:17,350
The red key shook between my fingers.

117
00:04:17,375 --> 00:04:19,902
From the desk, Lena called my name.

118
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:22,542
The receiver was still on its cradle.

119
00:04:22,567 --> 00:04:24,030
Please, Daniel. Pick up.

120
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:26,218
I reached for the antenna connector.

121
00:04:26,242 --> 00:04:28,730
The handle of the front
door began to turn.

122
00:04:28,755 --> 00:04:31,317
Slowly. I pulled the cable free.

123
00:04:31,342 --> 00:04:34,530
Every speaker in the station
screamed with my voice.

124
00:04:34,555 --> 00:04:36,142
I dropped the flashlight.

125
00:04:36,167 --> 00:04:39,130
In the blackness, something
heavy struck the front door.

126
00:04:39,155 --> 00:04:40,795
Then there was silence.

127
00:04:41,755 --> 00:04:44,005
I waited until I could
hear the rain again.

128
00:04:44,030 --> 00:04:45,780
The radio light was dead.

129
00:04:45,805 --> 00:04:47,292
The telephone was silent.

130
00:04:47,318 --> 00:04:48,730
Nothing stood at the window.

131
00:04:48,755 --> 00:04:51,780
I left through the back, climbed
into my car, and kept the headlights

132
00:04:51,805 --> 00:04:53,580
off until I reached the road.

133
00:04:53,605 --> 00:04:56,580
When the dashboard radio
lit up, I tore its fuse out.

134
00:04:56,605 --> 00:04:59,730
I drove down the mountain with
both hands locked on the wheel.

135
00:04:59,755 --> 00:05:03,055
At the first place my phone
found service, I called Lena.

136
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:04,492
It rang once.

137
00:05:04,518 --> 00:05:06,918
Then I ended the call
before she could answer.

138
00:05:06,942 --> 00:05:09,482
Whatever happens, don't let her answer.

139
00:05:10,010 --> 00:05:12,410
I finally understood that sentence.

140
00:05:12,435 --> 00:05:15,572
I had thought the voice was
warning me about the future.

141
00:05:15,597 --> 00:05:18,172
Maybe it was only teaching me what to do.

142
00:05:18,198 --> 00:05:21,660
Maybe it had needed a voice, and
a reason for me to open another

143
00:05:21,685 --> 00:05:25,710
line. I drove the rest of the
way without touching the phone

144
00:05:25,735 --> 00:05:25,975
.

145
00:05:26,985 --> 00:05:29,510
Lena's porch light was on when I arrived.

146
00:05:29,535 --> 00:05:31,010
Her front door stood open.

147
00:05:31,035 --> 00:05:32,948
I stopped at the bottom of the steps.

148
00:05:32,972 --> 00:05:35,872
She appeared in the hallway
wearing her blue sleep shirt.

149
00:05:35,898 --> 00:05:37,585
She looked past me, toward the road.

150
00:05:37,610 --> 00:05:39,085
Then back at my face.

151
00:05:39,110 --> 00:05:40,160
How did you get outside?

152
00:05:40,185 --> 00:05:43,060
she asked. I told her
not to say another word.

153
00:05:43,085 --> 00:05:45,772
From the upstairs bedroom,
my voice called down.

154
00:05:45,797 --> 00:05:47,598
Lena? Who are you talking to?

155
00:05:47,622 --> 00:05:48,935
She began to turn.

156
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:51,548
I caught her wrist and
pulled her onto the porch.

157
00:05:51,572 --> 00:05:54,338
Behind her, the telephone started ringing.

158
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:56,515
She looked at the phone in my hand.

159
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:57,890
The screen was black.

160
00:05:57,915 --> 00:05:59,228
I wasn't calling.

161
00:05:59,252 --> 00:06:01,740
Upstairs, bare feet crossed the floor.

162
00:06:01,765 --> 00:06:03,002
Slow steps.

163
00:06:03,028 --> 00:06:05,290
Then a man laughed with my voice.

164
00:06:05,315 --> 00:06:07,228
I had disconnected the antenna.

165
00:06:07,252 --> 00:06:09,640
I had never touched the telephone line.

166
00:06:09,665 --> 00:06:13,030
At the top of the stairs,
something knocked three times.
